{"strongs": "H2623", "word": "חָסִיד", "translit": "cha.sid", "root": "חנך", "morph": "H:A", "pos": "adjective masculine", "gloss": "kind, pious", "definition": "חָסִיד adjective masculine kind, pious (so, as denoting active practice of חֶסֶד , kindness, Thes MV De and most, compare קָצִיר , פָּקִיד etc.; > Hup on Ps 4:4 RVm who explained as passive reception of ׳ י 's חֶסֶד , compare שָֹׂכֹיר , אָסִיר etc.; its use as attribute of God Jer 3:12 ; Ps 145:17 , and the context Ps 12:1 ; Mic 7:2 etc., favour active sense) — ׳ ח Ps 4:4 + 9 t.; חֲסִידֶ֑ךָ Deut 33:8 ; Ps 89:20 חֲסִידְי֯ךָ Ps 16:10 plural חֲסִידִים Ps 149:1 ; Ps 149:5 suffix חֲסִידָ֑י Ps 50:5 חֲסִידָו֯ 1Sam 2:9 + 15 t. suffixes; — 1. kind: \\ \\ a. of man תתחסד ׳ עם ח with the kind thou shewest thyself kind 2Sam 22:26 = Ps 18:26 . \\ \\ b. of wing of ostrich אִם אֶבְרָה חֲסִידָה Job 39:13 is it a kindly pinion? possibly with play on חֲסִידָה feminine noun strok (is the ostrich kind like the stork?). \\ \\ c. of God, only Jer 3:12 ; Ps 145:17 . 2. pious, godly , either as exhibition of 'duteous love' toward God ( Che OP 378 ), or (in view of rarity of such passages as Hos 6:4 ; Hos 6:6 ; Jer 2:2 , and their possible ambiguity) because kindness , as prominent in the godly, comes to imply other attributes, and to be a designation of the godly character, piety: \\ \\ a. as adjective — גּוֺי לא חסיד a nation, not pious , = ungodly Ps 43:1 . \\ \\ b. elsewhere as substantive: singular, a pious man, the godly Ps 4:4 ; Ps 12:2 ; Ps 32:6 ; Ps 86:2 , || יָשָׁר Mic 7:2 ( thy ) pious one \\ \\ \\ ( s ) Ps 16:10 ( Kt plural), 1Sam 2:9 ( Qr plural) Prov 2:8 , אִישׁ חֲסִידֶ֑ךָ men of thy pious one Deut 33:8 (Moses, see Di ; others, the man, thy godly one , i.e. Levi); plural the pious, godly , those of the people who were faithful, devoted to God's service, only in Psalter and chiefly, if not entirely, in late Psalms Ps 149:1 ; Ps 149:5 his pious ones Ps 30:5 ; Ps 31:24 ; Ps 37:28 ; Ps 85:9 ; Ps 97:10 ; Ps 116:15 ; Ps 148:14 ; Ps 149:9 thy pious ones Ps 52:11 ; Ps 79:2 ; Ps 132:9 = 2Chr 6:41 ; Ps 145:10 my pious ones Ps 50:5 , her (Zion's) pious Ps 132:16 . — (In Maccabean age, συναγωγὴ Ἀσιδαίων denoted, technically, the party of the pious , who opposed the Hellenization of the Judaea, see 1 Macc 2:42; 7:13; 2 Macc 14:6 and Che OP 48, 56 ; so perhaps Ps 116:15 ; Ps 149:1 ; Ps 149:5 ; Ps 149:9 .)", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2966')\">BDB2966</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2623')\">H2623</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2965')\">BDB2965</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2967')\">BDB2967</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>חָסִיד</bdbheb> <b>adjective masculine</b> <highlightword>kind, pious</highlightword> (so, as denoting active practice of <bdbheb>חֶסֶד</bdbheb>, kindness, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Thes')\">Thes</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('MV')\">MV</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De</lookup> and most, compare <bdbheb>קָצִיר</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>פָּקִיד</bdbheb> etc.; &gt; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hup')\">Hup</lookup> on <ref ref=\"Ps 4:4\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(19,4,4)\">Ps 4:4</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('RV')\"><reflink>RVm</reflink></lookup> who explained as passive <highlight>reception</highlight> of <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb>'s <bdbheb>חֶסֶד</bdbheb>, compare <bdbheb>שָֹׂכֹיר</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אָסִיר</bdbheb> etc.; its use as attribute of God <ref ref=\"Jer 3:12\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(24,3,12)\">Jer 3:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 145:17\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"145\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"145\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(19,145,17)\">Ps 145:17</ref>, and the context <ref ref=\"Ps 12:1\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(19,12,1)\">Ps 12:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Mic 7:2\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(33,7,2)\">Mic 7:2</ref> etc., favour active sense) — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 4:4\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(19,4,4)\">Ps 4:4</ref> + 9 t.; <bdbheb>חֲסִידֶ֑ךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 33:8\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(5,33,8)\">Deut 33:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 89:20\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"89\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"89\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(19,89,20)\">Ps 89:20</ref> <bdbheb>חֲסִידְי֯ךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 16:10\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(19,16,10)\">Ps 16:10</ref> plural <bdbheb>חֲסִידִים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 149:1\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"149\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"149\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(19,149,1)\">Ps 149:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 149:5\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"149\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"149\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(19,149,5)\">Ps 149:5</ref> suffix <bdbheb>חֲסִידָ֑י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 50:5\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"50\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"50\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(19,50,5)\">Ps 50:5</ref> <bdbheb>חֲסִידָו֯</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 2:9\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(9,2,9)\">1Sam 2:9</ref> + 15 t. suffixes; — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>kind:</highlight> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> of man <bdbheb>תתחסד</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>עם ח</bdbheb> <highlight>with the kind thou shewest thyself kind</highlight> <ref ref=\"2Sam 22:26\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(10,22,26)\">2Sam 22:26</ref> = <ref ref=\"Ps 18:26\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(19,18,26)\">Ps 18:26</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> of wing of ostrich <bdbheb>אִם אֶבְרָה חֲסִידָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 39:13\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"39\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"39\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(18,39,13)\">Job 39:13</ref> <highlight>is it a kindly pinion?</highlight> possibly with play on <bdbheb>חֲסִידָה</bdbheb> feminine noun <highlight>strok</highlight> (is the ostrich kind like the stork?). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> of God, only <ref ref=\"Jer 3:12\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(24,3,12)\">Jer 3:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 145:17\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"145\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"145\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(19,145,17)\">Ps 145:17</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> <highlight>pious, godly</highlight>, either as exhibition of 'duteous love' toward God (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Che')\">Che<sup>OP 378</sup></lookup>), or (in view of rarity of such passages as <ref ref=\"Hos 6:4\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(28,6,4)\">Hos 6:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hos 6:6\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(28,6,6)\">Hos 6:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 2:2\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(24,2,2)\">Jer 2:2</ref>, and their possible ambiguity) because <highlight>kindness</highlight>, as prominent in the godly, comes to imply other attributes, and to be a designation of the godly character, <highlight>piety:</highlight> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> as adjective — <bdbheb>גּוֺי לא חסיד</bdbheb> <highlight>a nation, not pious</highlight>, = <highlight>ungodly</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ps 43:1\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"43\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"43\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(19,43,1)\">Ps 43:1</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> elsewhere as substantive: singular, <highlight>a pious man, the godly</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ps 4:4\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(19,4,4)\">Ps 4:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 12:2\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(19,12,2)\">Ps 12:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 32:6\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(19,32,6)\">Ps 32:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 86:2\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"86\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"86\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(19,86,2)\">Ps 86:2</ref>, || <bdbheb>יָשָׁר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Mic 7:2\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(33,7,2)\">Mic 7:2</ref> (<highlight>thy</highlight>) <highlight>pious one</highlight><br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;\\&emsp;(<highlight>s</highlight>) <ref ref=\"Ps 16:10\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(19,16,10)\">Ps 16:10</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Kt')\"><reflink>Kt</reflink></lookup> plural), <ref ref=\"1Sam 2:9\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(9,2,9)\">1Sam 2:9</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Qr')\"><reflink>Qr</reflink></lookup> plural) <ref ref=\"Prov 2:8\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(20,2,8)\">Prov 2:8</ref>, <bdbheb>אִישׁ חֲסִידֶ֑ךָ</bdbheb> <highlight>men of thy pious one</highlight> <ref ref=\"Deut 33:8\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(5,33,8)\">Deut 33:8</ref> (Moses, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di</lookup>; others, <highlight>the man, thy godly one</highlight>, i.e. Levi); plural <highlight>the pious, godly</highlight>, those of the people who were faithful, devoted to God's service, only in Psalter and chiefly, if not entirely, in late Psalms <ref ref=\"Ps 149:1\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"149\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"149\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(19,149,1)\">Ps 149:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 149:5\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"149\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"149\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(19,149,5)\">Ps 149:5</ref> <highlight>his pious ones</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ps 30:5\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(19,30,5)\">Ps 30:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 31:24\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(19,31,24)\">Ps 31:24</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 37:28\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"28\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"28\" onclick=\"bcv(19,37,28)\">Ps 37:28</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 85:9\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"85\" vBegi